+# TASK-031 round 12: narrow round 11's shadow check to the modules pytest reads its configuration with
+
+## Objective
+
+Fix the following confirmed defect: repair the named cause, nothing else. This increment is past the owner's three-round review ceiling. After round 11 the supervisor drew a by-class line on this subsystem: only a regression or a false kill on an ordinary project layout blocks. This round carries exactly that, two regressions on ordinary layouts, reported by both round 11's Review A and its security audit. **The supervisor's round-11 brief caused them** (`handoff/TASK-031-r11.md` Requirement 1 asked for the environment lookup). You implemented that brief as written. This round narrows the check; it does not reopen it. Every other finding of round 11's reviews is recorded in `docs/HARDENING.md` under TASK-031 and is not yours to fix.
+
+**Root cause, in one sentence.** `_refuse_if_copy_root_shadows_importable_module` (`bridge/cursor-bridge/mutation-run.py`, around :908-950) refuses any top-level module or regular package whose name is in `sys.stdlib_module_names`, in `sys.builtin_module_names`, or found by `importlib.util.find_spec` in the program's environment. Most of those names are never imported by pytest to find its configuration, so the refusal protects nothing and stops ordinary projects.
+
+**Evidence (round 11's Review A and security audit; convergent).**
+- A `test/` test package with `__init__.py` is refused: `find_spec("test")` finds CPython's own regression-test package `Lib/test`. Round 10 ran it.
+- The project's own package, found elsewhere by the environment (after `pip install .`, an editable install from another checkout, or another copy on `PYTHONPATH`), is refused: `demo` is refused. Round 10 ran it.
+- Two side effects come from the same branch. `find_spec("distutils")` runs setuptools' meta path finder inside the check (197 modules loaded). The origin exclusion under the working folder hides every installed module when the virtual environment lies inside the project.
+
+**Reproduction tests (red on round 11's code, 1d52cfd; must pass).** In `tests/test_mutation_run_supervisor.py`:
+- `test_task031_r11_a_top_level_name_shadowing_nothing_runs_its_mutant[test/__init__.py]` (refused today with "a top-level module test ...");
+- `test_task031_r12_the_projects_own_package_installed_elsewhere_runs_its_mutant` (refused today naming `demo`).
+
+`handoff/TASK-031.md` and `-r2.md` to `-r11.md` still govern everything this file does not change. Where an earlier brief disagrees with this file, this file wins. This round replaces `handoff/TASK-031-r11.md` Requirement 1's "shadows" test and Requirement 3, and lifts that brief's ban on "a fixed list of module names": the fixed list below is this round's decision.
+
+Satisfies:
+- R-041 (quoted whole in `handoff/TASK-031.md`). The clause at stake is "gives every mutant a result against the version the gate reads". A refusal of a project whose configuration pytest reads with the same code as the program gives that project no result at all.
+
+## Scope
+
+One brief carries one increment's scope; work that needs a second scope is a second brief, never a second section here.
+
+Files you may create or modify:
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/mutation-run.py (only `_refuse_if_copy_root_shadows_importable_module` and the module-level `import importlib.util` at :15; a module-level constant holding the list, read only by that function, is allowed)
+- tests/test_mutation_run.py (no new test is needed. Change the builder's `test_task031_r11_extension_suffix_shadow_refused` only if it must change, and say why in the report)
